      "id": 1,
      "text": "Moreland Hills was incorporated as a village in 1929, taking the southeast quadrant of former Orange Township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moreland_Hills%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village sits at the junction of State Route 87 and the Chagrin River, where settlement began in 1815.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moreland_Hills%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Moreland Hills is home to Hiram House, a state historical landmark and the nation's second settlement house after Chicago's Hull House.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moreland_Hills%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1831, the Orange Conference of the LDS Church met in what is now Moreland Hills, featuring leaders Joseph Smith, Sidney Rigdon, and Oliver Cowdery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moreland_Hills%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Actress and comedian Vanessa Bayer, known for Saturday Night Live, hails from Moreland Hills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
